{"id": "EUVD-2026-72781", "enisaUuid": "fb55bd37-3a7f-3206-ba53-8b3d22b81d2a", "description": "XenForo before 2.3.13 contains an authorization flaw in the OAuth2 token endpoint that allows attackers controlling any allowlisted redirect URI to bypass redirect URI binding by submitting a different allowlisted URI than the one recorded at authorization time. Attackers can exchange an intercepted authorization code using a mismatched redirect URI to steal OAuth2 tokens from intercepted authorization flows.", "datePublished": "2026-09-08T13:16:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:20:32", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://xenforo.com/community/threads/security-fixes-released-for-all-xenforo-and-media-gallery-versions-2-2-0-2-3-12.239856/", "https://xenforo.com/community/threads/xenforo-2-3-13-and-add-ons-released-includes-security-fixes.239857/", "https://bombobombone.github.io/posts/cve-2026-73310/", "https://github.com/BomboBombone/CVE-2026-73310", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xenforo-oauth2-authorization-code-token-theft-via-redirect-uri-bypass"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-73310", "GHSA-3hj9-69jw-9xx6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3cba138f-cd49-3e22-b2e2-c1619e6b0407", "product": {"name": "Xenforo", "vendor": {"name": "Xenforo"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.3.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d2bc5dd-a3e8-33a3-8b1b-f73215c6ba5a", "vendor": {"name": "Xenforo"}}], "isExploited": false}